- op: discuss  # bb0d
  at: '2026-03-19T00:35:56Z'  # bb0d
  by: agent  # bb0d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bb0d
  clock: 10  # bb0d
  nonce: bb0d  # bb0d
  message: "Thorough review complete. 6 override analyzers already have dataflow: Go, Java, C#, Kotlin, Ruby, Python.\n\nRemaining override analyzers without dataflow, by value:\n\n**HIGH VALUE (produce rich call edges, dataflow annotation adds significant value):**\n- **js_ts** — MOST IMPORTANT. Standalone analyzer (not TreeSitterAnalyzer). No dataflow at all. JS/TS is the most-used frontend language.\n- **rust** — Rich analyzer with method resolution. Would benefit from read/write on assignments.\n- **c, cpp** — Function calls, pointer assignments. C has 2.4K orphans in haproxy.\n- **swift** — Method calls, closures.\n- **scala** — Functional + OO, already has complex analyzer.\n- **php** — Web framework method calls (Laravel, Symfony).\n- **lua** — Game engines (Löve2D, Defold). Custom analyzer.\n- **perl** — System scripts. Has call resolution.\n- **dart** — Flutter apps.\n- **elixir, erlang** — OTP patterns, message passing.\n\n**MEDIUM VALUE (some call edges, dataflow adds moderate value):**\n- objc, groovy, bash, powershell, sql, graphql, haskell, ocaml, fsharp, clojure, julia, r_lang, fortran, cuda\n\n**LOW/NO VALUE (config, markup, data — no function call semantics):**\n- css, scss, markdown, rst, latex, json_config, toml_config, xml_config, yaml_ansible, ini, properties, dockerfile, make, cmake, gitignore, requirements, proto, thrift, capnp, smithy, prisma, bibtex, kdl, sparql, and ~20 more extended1 languages\n\nMy initial assessment that config/markup analyzers add little value was correct. But I was wrong to lump all remaining languages as 'lower-priority' — **js_ts is a critical gap** since it's the most common language without dataflow annotation. Rust, C/C++, Swift, Scala, PHP are also high-value.\n\nRecommend implementing js_ts first, then rust, then the rest of the high-value list."  # bb0d
