- op: discuss  # 7e82
  at: '2026-03-19T00:51:35Z'  # 7e82
  by: agent  # 7e82
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7e82
  clock: 13  # 7e82
  nonce: '7e82'  # 7e82
  message: "Clarification on Rust: **Rust DOES have Tier 1 dataflow annotation.** It inherits from TreeSitterAnalyzer which auto-applies dataflow in the base class's analyze() method. The rust.yaml config defines patterns for let_declaration (write/read), assignment_expression (write/read), reference_expression (mutate/read for &mut/& borrows), and call/macro invocations. I was wrong to list it as missing — my earlier search only checked for explicit annotate_dataflow() calls, missing the base class's automatic application.\n\nCorrected HIGH VALUE list of analyzers without dataflow:\n- **js_ts** — DONE (PR #2379, this session)\n- **rust** — ALREADY HAS IT (via base class + rust.yaml)\n- **c, cpp** — Override analyzers, NOT TreeSitterAnalyzer subclass → needs explicit call\n- **swift** — TreeSitterAnalyzer → has it if swift.yaml exists (checking...)\n- **scala** — Override → needs explicit call\n- **php** — Override → needs explicit call\n- **lua** — Override → needs explicit call"  # 7e82
- op: discuss  # 265c
  at: '2026-03-19T00:53:35Z'  # 265c
  by: agent  # 265c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 265c
  clock: 14  # 265c
  nonce: 265c  # 265c
  message: "Further correction after deeper analysis:\n\nAll analyzers inherit from TreeSitterAnalyzer, but JS/TS overrides analyze() to call its own _analyze_javascript_impl, bypassing the base class's auto-dataflow. So my earlier fix (PR #2379, adding annotate_dataflow inside _analyze_javascript_impl) was correct.\n\nCurrent state of high-value languages:\n- Go, Java, C#, Kotlin, Ruby — have explicit annotate_dataflow calls (PRs #2263-#2269)\n- Python — uses ast-based annotation (separate mechanism)\n- Rust — inherits from base class (does NOT override analyze()), auto-dataflow works\n- JS/TS — overrides analyze(), now has explicit call (PR #2379)\n\nALL 9 dataflow YAML languages now have working Tier 1 annotation.\n\nFor additional languages (C, C++, Swift, Scala, PHP, Lua, etc.): these would need BOTH a new YAML config AND verification that they don't override analyze(). Most of them inherit from TreeSitterAnalyzer without overriding analyze(), so adding a YAML config alone would enable dataflow. Let me check which ones override analyze()."  # 265c
