  message: "Complete analysis of override vs. base class flow:\n\n**Analyzers that call super().analyze() (base class dataflow auto-works):**\nelixir, erlang, markdown, perl, requirements\n\n**Analyzers that BYPASS base class (need explicit annotate_dataflow if YAML exists):**\nc, cmake, cpp, css, csharp, dockerfile, go, java, json_config, js_ts, kotlin, latex, lua, make, matlab, meson, objc, php, proto, puppet, purescript, r_lang, racket, robot, rst, ruby, scheme, scss, starlark, svelte, thrift, toml_config, vue, xml_config, yaml_ansible\n\n**Analyzers that DON'T override analyze() (all others — base class auto-works if YAML exists):**\n~70 analyzers in common/extended1 packages: ada, agda, apex, asm, bash, dart, fsharp, etc.\n\n**Current coverage (languages with both YAML + working dataflow):**\nGo ✓, Java ✓, C# ✓, Kotlin ✓, Ruby ✓, JS/TS ✓, Rust ✓, Python ✓ (ast-based), TypeScript ✓ (via javascript.yaml + JS analyzer)\n\n**Next highest-value additions (need YAML config creation):**\n1. C/C++ — assignments and function calls\n2. Swift — let/var declarations\n3. Scala — val/var declarations\n4. PHP — assignments\n5. Lua — local declarations\n\nFor these, I need to create language-specific YAML files defining AST node types for assignments, deletions, and calls. The tree-sitter node type names differ per grammar."  # 861f
